        <fig id="article-820.image.f3" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Glymphatic System. The illustration shows glymphatic fluid flow (white arrows) along periarterial and perivenous pathways. Labeled structures include the dura, meningeal lymphatics, subarachnoid space, brain parenchyma, arterial and venous circulation, and aquaporin 4 channels mediating influx and efflux. Contributed by Konstantinos Margetis MD, PhD</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="Glymphatics" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
